body:
`loadLanguage` can return non-translation shapes (e.g., the full `{ data: ... }` envelope, `null`, or an array) because the fallback returns `json` unvalidated. `I18nProvider` passes the returned value into `i18nInstance.addResourceBundle`, which expects a plain object of translation keys; returning the envelope (or non-object) can silently break i18n and may prevent retries due to `loadedAppLangs`. Consider only returning a plain object translation map (unwrap `data.translations` when it’s a non-null, non-array object; otherwise return `{}` and optionally log/throw).
```suggestion
    if (
      json &&
      typeof json === 'object' &&
      !Array.isArray(json) &&
      'data' in json &&
      json.data &&
      typeof json.data === 'object' &&
      !Array.isArray(json.data) &&
      'translations' in json.data &&
      json.data.translations &&
      typeof json.data.translations === 'object' &&
      !Array.isArray(json.data.translations)
    ) {
      return json.data.translations as Record<string, unknown>;
    }

    // Fallback: mock server / local dev returns flat translation objects.
    // Only accept non-null, non-array plain objects as translation maps.
    if (json && typeof json === 'object' && !Array.isArray(json)) {
      return json as Record<string, unknown>;
    }

    console.warn(
      `[i18n] Invalid translations payload for '${lang}', expected an object map but received:`,
      json,
    );
    return {};
```
